# PSR-8c — Governance files inventory

## Intent

Inventory what PSR-8 / PSR-9 require for publishable governance **without**
choosing a license or adding legal files in this wave (Architect + counsel).

## Required trio (SoT)

| File | Present | Notes |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| `LICENSE` / `LICENSE.md` | no | Blocks public clone claims |
| `SECURITY.md` | no | Vulnerability disclosure path missing |
| `CONTRIBUTING.md` | no | Contribution / DCO / CLA undecided |

## Related gaps

| Asset | Present | Notes |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| `CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md` | no | Optional but listed in SoT governance |
| `CODEOWNERS` | probe | May exist under `.github/` — see inventory yaml |
| `GOVERNANCE.md` | no | Program-level decision record |
| Package `license` fields | sparse | Several `UNLICENSED` (finance/booking contracts) |
| Publication model | undecided | full OSS vs open-core vs source-available (PSR-8a) |

## Non-goals

- Writing/choosing LICENSE text
- Adding SECURITY/CONTRIBUTING content
- Claiming L-GOV closed

## Smoke

```bash
node scripts/ops/psr-8c-governance-files-inventory-smoke.mjs
```

## Next

Architect chooses publication model + license → `PSR-8c1-governance-files-land`
(doc-first templates). Or YES/accept packs / `PSR-8b1` rename.
